# The same cy::demo::Health values, written by a build whose field order was different, and carrying
# one field this build has never heard of. Task 1.2.5.
#
# This is the golden that proves the identity model rather than the encoding. Nothing here depends
# on declaration order or on a byte offset — the record addresses fields by FieldId — so it loads
# into today's struct and produces the same values as health_canonical.hex.
#
# FieldId 200 is a field that no build in this tree declares. A reader skips it: its number is
# retired in the manifest and will never be issued to anything else, which is what makes skipping it
# safe rather than a silent misread.

